{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01HQs6v9NLMhUTy8938Ki32p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture of what I need to implement. Let me plan the approach:\n\n**Task**: Create `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` implementing the DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests function.\n\n**Key requirements from the task description (R1-R4)**:\n- R1: DiffTest struct with fields for input args, stdin, env vars, expected exit code, expected output\n- R2: Function to execute both Go and reference binaries with identical inputs\n- R3: Compare stdout, stderr, exit code byte-for-byte with normalization support\n- R4: Report divergence with input args, expected (reference) output, actual (Go) output\n\n\n- R1.1: DiffTest struct with Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n- R1.2: Stdin nil = EOF\n- R1.3: Env nil = inherit + defaults; non-nil = merge into inherited env\n- R1.4: NormalizeFunc type alias\n- R2.1: RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests) with subtests\n- R2.2: Capture stdout, stderr, exit code independently\n- R2.3: Configurable timeout\n\n, default 10s\n- R2.4: No output during passing test\n- R2.5: WorkDir field, default t.TempDir()\n- R2.6: LC_ALL=C default\n- R3.1-R3.6: Comparison and reporting\n- R4.1-R4.4: Normalization hooks, TimestampNormalizer, ComposeNormalizers\n- R5.1-R5.2: ExpectedFiles comparison\n\nThe requirements cover the DiffTest struct with all necessary fields, the RunDiffTests function that executes tests with independent capture of outputs and exit codes, configurable timeouts defaulting to 10 seconds, and a working directory that defaults to a temp directory. The spec also includes normalization hooks for flexible output comparison and file-based assertions, with detailed divergence reporting that shows the triggering input alongside expected and actual results. All of this needs to compile and pass the build check.\n\nNow I'm ready to start implementing the difftest.go file, making sure to follow the PRD requirements precisely and verify the directory structure exists first.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3652,"cache_read_input_tokens":51177,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3652},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a46b6b9b-d57f-47f4-a3f4-f28d20fc918e","uuid":"16e1c00d-cd59-42d3-8273-5c1a363311fc"}
